# public/banners.json is GENERATED from the registry comment block in
# src/lib/buildingImages.js by scripts/gen-banners-json.mjs, and `npm run banners:check`
# re-generates it and compares the BYTES against the committed copy.
#
# The generator writes LF. On Windows, git's default `core.autocrlf=true` checks the file
# out with CRLF, so the two differ by one byte per line and the check reports
#
#     public/banners.json is stale. Run: node scripts/gen-banners-json.mjs
#
# on a clean `main` with nothing wrong. Measured 2026-10-25: strip the carriage returns from
# both copies and the SHA-256 is identical — the content was never stale. CI runs on Linux,
# where there are no CRs, so it has always passed there; this only ever cried wolf locally,
# and the cost was a developer regenerating a file that did not need regenerating and then
# carrying a phantom modification in `git status`.
#
# Pinning the file to LF makes the checked-out bytes match what the generator writes, on
# every platform.
#
# ⚠ Existing clones already hold the CRLF copy. One `git add --renormalize public/banners.json`
# (or deleting the file and `git checkout -- public/banners.json`) refreshes it; new clones
# are correct immediately.
public/banners.json text eol=lf
